---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.config';
---

<PageLayout
  title={'Terms & Conditions'}
  description={`The terms governing use of ${SITE.name} — acceptable use, intellectual property, AI content disclaimers, directory listings and limitation of liability.`}
  lede="The rules for using this site."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-08-02')}
>
  <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-warning)]/40 bg-[var(--color-warning)]/10 p-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">
    <strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Note:</strong> these terms are written in good faith
    and describe how this site is actually operated, but they are not legal advice. If you
    operate this site, have them reviewed by a qualified practitioner in your jurisdiction.
  </div>

  <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    By accessing <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong> you agree to these terms. If you do not
    agree, do not use the site. These terms apply to every part of {SITE.name}, including
    the article archive, the <a href="/tools/">tool directory</a>, the
    <a href="/agents/">agent directory</a>, the <a href="/prompts/">prompt library</a> and
    the <a href="/resources/">resources</a> section.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Purpose of the content</h2>
  <p>
    All content is published for <strong>informational and educational purposes</strong>.
    It is general information about AI models, tools and techniques — not professional,
    legal, financial, tax, medical or engineering advice, and not a substitute for an
    assessment of your own systems, contracts or obligations by a qualified practitioner.
  </p>

  <h2>3. AI-specific content disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    Artificial intelligence is a fast-moving subject. Model versions, context limits,
    pricing tiers, rate limits, license terms and vendor policies change frequently and
    often without notice. An article that was accurate on its publication date may be out
    of date by the time you read it.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Always verify model capabilities, pricing and license terms against the vendor's own
      current documentation before making a commercial or architectural decision.
    </li>
    <li>
      Outputs from AI systems can be wrong, biased or fabricated. Any code, prompt or
      workflow published here should be tested and reviewed by a competent human before it
      touches production, customer data or anything with money attached.
    </li>
    <li>
      Nothing published here is a guarantee that a model, agent or tool will behave the way
      it did during our testing. Model behavior changes when the vendor changes the model.
    </li>
    <li>
      You are responsible for complying with the terms of service of any third-party AI
      provider you use, and with any law that applies to how you use its output.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Scrape, mirror or bulk-republish the content, including for the purpose of training a model, without written permission.</li>
    <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload or compromise the site or its infrastructure.</li>
    <li>Use the content to build a competing directory or dataset by automated extraction.</li>
    <li>Misrepresent our content as your own, or present a mention or listing as an endorsement of your product.</li>
    <li>Submit false, misleading or spam entries to the directories or the prompt library.</li>
    <li>Use the site in any way that breaks the law where you are.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Articles, artwork, ratings and site design are &copy; {new Date().getFullYear()}
    {' '}{SITE.organization.legalName} unless stated otherwise. You may quote short extracts
    with clear attribution and a link to the source article. Republishing whole articles, or
    reproducing the directory data in bulk, requires written permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    Code samples and prompts published in articles and in the
    <a href="/prompts/">prompt library</a> may be used freely in your own projects, with no
    attribution required and no warranty attached. Third-party names, logos and trademarks
    referenced remain the property of their owners; their use here is nominative and does
    not imply any affiliation or endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Submissions</h2>
  <p>
    If you send us a tip, a directory submission, a prompt or feedback, you confirm you have
    the right to send it and you grant us a non-exclusive, royalty-free license to publish
    and adapt it as part of the site. We are not obliged to publish anything you send, and
    we may edit submissions for accuracy, length and house style. We do not treat
    unsolicited submissions as confidential.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Third-party links and directory listings</h2>
  <p>
    We link to vendors, documentation, repositories and research. We do not control those
    destinations and are not responsible for their content, accuracy, availability,
    security or terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    A listing in the tool or agent directory is an editorial judgment made at a point in
    time. It is not an endorsement, a certification, a guarantee of quality or safety, and
    not a recommendation to purchase. Listings are not paid for. Some outbound links may be
    affiliate links, which is explained in the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>. Your
    dealings with any third party are entirely between you and that third party.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Availability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided "as is" and "as available". We do not guarantee uninterrupted
    access, and we may change, update, suspend or remove content, listings or entire
    sections at any time without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied,
    including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy and
    non-infringement. We do not warrant that the content is complete, current or free of
    error, nor that the site is free of harmful components. See the full
    <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, {SITE.organization.legalName} is not liable for
    any indirect, incidental, consequential, special or punitive damages, or for any loss of
    data, profits, revenue, goodwill or business, arising from your use of this site,
    reliance on its content, or your dealings with any third-party tool or vendor referenced
    here. Where liability cannot be excluded, it is limited to the amount you paid us to
    access the content, which for the public site is nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Indemnity</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify us against claims arising from your misuse of the site, your
    breach of these terms, or your infringement of a third party's rights.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the site changes. The revised version takes effect when it
    is published, and the "last updated" date above will change. Continued use after that
    point constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of
    {SITE.organization.address ? ` ${SITE.organization.address.countryName}` : ' the country in which the publisher is established'},
    and any dispute is subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of
    {SITE.organization.address
      ? ` ${SITE.organization.address.locality}, ${SITE.organization.address.countryName}`
      : ' that place'}. Nothing in these terms removes a mandatory consumer protection
    right you have under the law of your own country of residence.
  </p>
  <!--
    Owner: this now names the operating company's jurisdiction from site.config.ts. If the
    publishing entity is registered somewhere other than its operating location, or you
    want a specific court named, have a lawyer set the exact wording before you rely on it.
  -->

  <h2>14. Severability</h2>
  <p>
    If any provision of these terms is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions stay in
    force.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.organization.email}`}>{SITE.organization.email}</a>, or via the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
